      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a square, we can use the formula: Area = side × side. We know that the perimeter of a square is 32 ft, so we can set up an equation to find the side of the square. \n\n32 ft = 4 × side\nDivide both sides of the equation by 4 to isolate the side:\n\n32 ft / 4 = side\n8 ft = side\nNow that we know the side of the square is 8 ft, we can find the area:\n\nArea = 8 ft × 8 ft\nArea = 64 ft²\n\nThe area of the square is 64 square feet.\nThe answer is: 64",
